    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14966" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dūrăcĭnus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		durus-acinus, orig. of the grape, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>hard-berried</i>, <i>hard</i> (only fit for eating): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">uva,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato R.
					R. 7, 2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 14, 1, 3, § 14</span></i>; Suct.
				<i><span class="en">Aug.
			76</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 13, 22</span></i>; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vites,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					3, 2, 1</span></i>
			.—<b>Transf.</b>, of other fruits: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">persica,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					15, 12, 11, § 39</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. 15, 28, 34, § 113</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Pall. Febr. 25, 32</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cerasa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					15, 25, 30, § 103</span></i>
			.</div>
